%% Ingestion pipeline as actually implemented (scripts/bootstrap_corpus.py).
%% Embeddings are OpenAI text-embedding-3-small (1536-dim), not Titan: the
%% local fastembed/ONNX path was ~100x slower and Titan's dimensions do not
%% match the 1536-dim Pinecone index.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant EB as EventBridge (weekly cron)
    participant B as bootstrap_corpus.py
    participant CC as chunk_cache/ (local, per-ticker)
    participant E as edgar_client.py
    participant S3R as S3 (finrag-raw-filings)
    participant H as html_processor.py
    participant C as chunker.py
    participant Sy as sync_pinecone.py
    participant OA as OpenAI (text-embedding-3-small)
    participant PC as Pinecone (finrag-filings, 1536-dim)
    participant S3P as S3 (finrag-processed-filings)

    EB->>B: trigger ingestion

    loop for each of 72 tickers
        B->>CC: cache hit for {ticker}.json?
        alt already ingested
            CC-->>B: cached chunks (skip -- makes the run resumable)
        else not yet ingested
            B->>E: get_cik_for_ticker(ticker)
            E->>E: GET sec.gov/files/company_tickers.json
            Note over E: lists CURRENT registrants only; acquired or<br/>renamed firms (SQ->XYZ, ATVI, FL) fall back<br/>to CIK_OVERRIDES so their filings stay reachable
            E->>E: GET data.sec.gov/submissions/CIK{cik}.json

            loop for each 10-K / 10-Q
                E->>E: GET sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/...
                E->>S3R: store {ticker}/{form}/{date}.htm
                E-->>H: filing HTML
                H->>H: BeautifulSoup (lxml) text blocks
                H->>H: pandas table extraction (structure preserved)
                H-->>C: {text_blocks, tables, metadata}
                C->>C: chunk parent 1500w / child 400w / one per table
                C->>C: chunk_id = sha256(ticker|form|period|type|section|text)[:32]
                Note over C: content-addressed, NOT uuid4 -- re-ingest must<br/>overwrite rather than duplicate, and BM25 ids<br/>must equal Pinecone ids for merge dedup to work
                C-->>Sy: chunks
                Sy->>Sy: split into <=150k-token, <=2048-item batches
                Note over Sy: token count via tiktoken, not chars/4.<br/>OpenAI bills ~1.24x the local count, so an<br/>unsplit batch 400s and drops a whole filing
                Sy->>OA: embeddings.create(batch)
                OA-->>Sy: 1536-dim vectors
                Sy->>PC: upsert(id, vector, metadata)
            end

            alt every filing succeeded
                B->>CC: write {ticker}.json
            else any filing failed
                B->>B: record failure, write NO cache file
                Note over B: a partial cache would read as "done" on the<br/>next run -- this is how 20 filings went missing
            end
        end
    end

    B->>CC: read every cached ticker
    Note over B: BM25 is built over the WHOLE corpus, not just the<br/>tickers seen this run -- building from one run's<br/>chunks is what left the index covering 29 of 50
    B->>B: stream chunks one ticker file at a time into SQLite FTS5
    Note over B: 568 MB peak -- the old in-memory rank-bm25 build peaked<br/>at 7.5 GB and needed a temporary EC2 box
    B->>S3P: upload keyword/index.sqlite (~900 MB)
    B->>B: exit 1 if any ticker failed or is uncovered
    Note over PC,S3P: corpus ready: 164,092 chunks / 70 companies
